WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:07.649
A lot of people think China is taking over
the world.

00:00:07.649 --> 00:00:10.330
They think that because China has a big economy.

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:14.290
And they're said to be growing still pretty
fast, much faster than the U.S., two or three

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:15.330
times faster.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:19.320
What's missed there is what's growing even
faster than China's economy is China's debt.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:23.090
Since 2008, the U.S. has borrowed a lot of
money, but China has borrowed about three

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:24.090
times as much.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.890
We're talking about $20 trillion or so.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:30.340
The worst performance in world history on
debt.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:34.840
You go one step down to the industry part,
China does have a very big industrial sector,

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.720
probably biggest in the world, bigger than
the United States.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.450
And they're saying it's growing at 6% which
is a pretty fast clip.

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:44.250
But what they don't say is that rail freight,
which is how you'd carry a lot of the industrial

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.430
production, is actually shrinking.

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:49.620
They don't say that port freight, which is
another way to carry industrial production,

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.700
is growing only about half the speed of industrial
production.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.489
So one possibility is China is building a
lot of stuff.

00:00:55.489 --> 00:00:56.649
But it's not going anywhere.

00:00:56.649 --> 00:00:57.649
It's just sitting.

00:00:57.649 --> 00:01:00.730
It's not being sold which means the companies
that build it aren't making money.

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:03.100
And guess what companies that don't make money
have to do?

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.100
They have to borrow.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.939
It gets us back to the debt.

00:01:06.939 --> 00:01:08.560
So is the bald guy right?

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:12.329
Let me know in the comments section, and let
us know what other topics you want AEI scholars

00:01:12.329 --> 00:01:13.830
to cover in 60 seconds.

